-- title:
--   Branch germs read as Gauss residues on X₀(N₀)_{κ_A}
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0 \ne 0$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbf Q}$ lying over $q$ (i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$), and a lift $\rho : R_q \to A$ of the structure map $R_q \to \overline{\mathbf Q}$; let $\mathfrak P$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`, and assume the residue field $\kappa_A$ of $A$ is algebraically closed of characteristic $q$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with an isomorphism $e_O$ onto $A \cap \overline{\mathbf Q}^{I_A}$ (the inertia-fixed subfield cut by $A$), with maximal ideal generated by $q$, equipped with a structure map $\rho_O : R_q \to O$ compatible with $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ through $e_O$, and with $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa_A$ given by $o \mapsto \mathrm{residue}(e_O(o))$. Let $P$ be a place specialisation of $A$ at level $N_0$ attached to modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence and to the Hecke integrality hypotheses $h\alpha, h\beta$, and $R$ a prolongation tuple for $P$, with its two regular prolongations $R.R_1, R.R_2$ of $A$ to $\overline{\mathbf Q}$-modular function field of level $N_0q$ and residue maps $R.\mathrm{residue}_1, R.\mathrm{residue}_2$ into `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa_A\, N_0$, the $\kappa_A$-subfield of Laurent series generated by the reductions of $j$ and $j(N_0 q)$. Assume the fibre `DRLevel.fibre0` of $X_0(N_0)$ over $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O$ and the base change $\mathfrak X_O = X(N_0q) \times_{R_q} \operatorname{Spec} O$ are integral schemes, and let $\varphi$ be a ring homomorphism from the function field of $\mathfrak X_O$ to the $\overline{\mathbf Q}$-modular function field of level $N_0q$ pinned on constants ($h\varphi O$: germs at the first branch point coming from $a \in O$ go to the image of $a$ in $\overline{\mathbf Q}$) and on the $j$-finite chart ($h\varphi j$: the Laurent expansion of $\varphi$ of a germ of $a \in$ `chartAlgFin` $(N_0q)\,q$ is the coefficientwise image of the expansion of $a$). Write $\xi_i$ ($i = 0,1$) for the image of the generic point of `fibre0` under $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{comp}\,i$ followed by `DRLevel.bcMap`, and assume that every germ at $\xi_0$ has $\varphi$-image in $R.R_1.\mathrm{integers}$ and every germ at $\xi_1$ has $\varphi$-image in $R.R_2.\mathrm{integers}$, and that $\xi_i$ coincides with the image of the generic point of $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{Mfib}(\kappa_A, \mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O).C$ under $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{efib}$ followed by the same map. The conclusion is the conjunction, for $i = 0$ and $i = 1$, of: for every germ $u$ in the stalk of $\mathfrak X_O$ at $\xi_i$, transporting $u$ along the equality of points and applying the stalk map of $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{efib} \gg \mathfrak P.\mathrm{comp}\,i \gg$ `bcMap` at the generic point of $\mathrm{Mfib}.C$, then the inverse $\mathrm{Mfib}.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$ of the function-field identification of the fibre curve model, yields the same element of `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa_A\, N_0$ as $R.\mathrm{residue}_1$ (for $i = 0$), respectively $R.\mathrm{residue}_2$ (for $i = 1$), applied to $\varphi(u)$ with its integrality witness.
--
--   This is the dictionary comparing the two descriptions of the characteristic-$q$ fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model at level $\Gamma_0(N_0q)$: on each of the two branches, isomorphic copies of $X_0(N_0)_{\kappa_A}$, reading a germ at the generic point through the function-field identification of the package's fibre curve model is the same as taking the residue of its $\varphi$-image along the corresponding Gauss prolongation $R_1$, respectively its Atkin–Lehner transport $R_2$. It is used in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.nodeResidue_eq_zero_iff_and_ord_eq_of_specializes_of_mem_maximalIdeal`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.nodeResidue_eq_zero_iff_and_ord_eq_of_specializes_of_mem_maximalIdeal), where the vanishing of the node parameter and the orders of functions at the supersingular points are computed.
